- airConJobMode: "COOL"
- targetTemperature: 22
- powerSaveEnabled: true
- windStrength: "HIGH"
- relativeHourToStart: 1
- relativeMinuteToStart: 30

Everything else defaults. So we need to call the function ThinQ_Connect with body containing those fields.

We need to produce a function call. The function signature: ThinQ_Connect(body: { ... }). So we need to output a JSON object with the body. The assistant should call the function. According to guidelines, we should not provide additional text. Just the function call. So we produce:

{
  "body": {
    "airConJobMode": "COOL",
    "targetTemperature": 22,
    "powerSaveEnabled": true,
    "windStrength": "HIGH",
    "relativeHourToStart": 1,
    "relativeMinuteToStart": 30
  }
}

But we need to wrap it in the function call. The tool invocation format: 
{
  "name": "ThinQ_Connect",
  "arguments": { ... }
}

So we produce:

{
  "name": "ThinQ_Connect",
  "arguments": {
    "body": {
      "airConJobMode": "COOL",
      "targetTemperature": 22,
      "powerSaveEnabled": true,
      "windStrength": "HIGH",
      "relativeHourToStart": 1,
      "relativeMinuteToStart": 30
    }
  }
}

